WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Until September 2025, Americans
buying a qualifying new electric

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.440
car could claim a federal tax
credit of up to 7,500 dollars.

3
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.010
Other subsidies work the other way around.

4
00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:17.030
The government pays firms a fixed
amount for every unit they make.

5
00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:18.950
The money goes to the firm.

6
00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:21.070
So does the firm keep it?

7
00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:23.590
Or do buyers see a lower price?

8
00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:26.800
When a government pays firms
for every item they make,

9
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.560
who ends up with the money?

10
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.040
In this mission, you'll shift
supply down by the subsidy

11
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.700
and find the area the government pays for.

12
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.350
Then you'll predict what
happens in a graph lab,

13
00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.410
and move a slider to check.

14
00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:42.530
Your mission: find out who
ends up with the money.
